//~ compile_fail(backend)
//~ error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch

// NEGATIVE (must FAIL to compile): take the WRITE lock and release it as a
// READER. The mirror image of `negative_wunlock_after_rlock.kz`, and the reason
// this lift spends two phantom states on the hold rather than one.
//
// `read.release` accepts only <!reading>, minted only by `read.acquire`.
//
// WHAT THE C DOES INSTEAD. `uk_rwlock_runlock` asserts `rwl->nactive > 0`
// (rwlock.c:98) and then decrements. Called while a writer holds the lock,
// `nactive` goes from -1 to **-2**, and from there:
//
//   * `uk_rwlock_rlock` waits on `nactive >= 0` (rwlock.c:58) — never true again.
//   * `uk_rwlock_wlock` waits on `nactive == 0` (rwlock.c:76) — never true again.
//
// Nothing ever clears it, because the only two writers of `nactive` back to a
// sane value are the very calls that are now blocked. The lock is permanently
// dead. With asserts off, the symptom is a hang at some LATER acquire, in
// whichever thread happens to reach it first — arbitrarily far in time and in
// call stack from the line that caused it.
//
// The two states are not decoration around a symmetric pair. `runlock` and
// `wunlock` are two different operations that share a signature, and the type is
// the only place the difference can live.
//
// EXPECTED: error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch: expected
//           'unikraft.lock:reading' but got 'unikraft.lock:writing!'
//           for argument 'lock'

// The `unikraft` namespace is declared here, not inherited: koruc's built-in
// alias probes the sibling koru-libs CHECKOUT, so in a worktree this file would
// otherwise compile against main's lifts instead of the ones beside it.
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/../..
}

~import unikraft/lock
~import std/io

~unikraft/lock:probe
| ready proof |> unikraft/lock:create(proof.locks)
    | lock guard |> unikraft/lock:write.acquire(lock: guard): exclusive
        |> unikraft/lock:read.release(lock: exclusive): done
            |> std/io:print.ln("should never get here")
            |> unikraft/lock:destroy(lock: done)
    | unavailable why |> std/io:print.ln("create failed: {{ why:s }}")
| unsupported why |> std/io:print.ln("uk_rwlock layout refused: {{ why:s }}")
